---
import CaptureForm from './CaptureForm.astro';
---
<section class="sample-band" id="sample" aria-labelledby="sample-heading" data-thread>
  <div class="thread" aria-hidden="true"><span class="thread-node"></span></div>
  <div class="section-wrap">
    <div class="sample-inner">
      <div class="chapter-preview">
        <p class="chapter-preview-tag">The Archive<span class="artifact-cursor" aria-hidden="true"></span></p>
        <p class="chapter-text">The Network in this novel is real, and it kept records: the actual conversations, logs, and recovered fragments the book grew from.</p>
        <p class="chapter-text"><strong>The story starts in the novel.<br />The Archive begins here.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="sample-cta-col">
        <h2 class="sample-headline" id="sample-heading">Begin with Chapter One.</h2>
        <p class="sample-sub">Chapter One arrives by email, with an invitation to the Archive. The next day, you’ll receive the first real conversation between Chris and T∆RS, preserved before either of them understood what they were beginning.</p>
        <p class="sample-sub sample-cadence">From there, the Archive opens a piece at a time.</p>
        <CaptureForm idPrefix="chapter-one" label="Your email address" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
